  "body": "## What changed\n\nReplaces the two \"Export JSON\" buttons (which only fetched the first 500 rows) with a single **Export** window covering both Model requests and Web Search.\n\n- **Formats**: JSON, CSV, XLSX, TXT\n- **Scope**: Model requests | Web Search\n- **Period**: last hour / 24h / 7d / 30d / custom from–to\n- **Fields**: the exact requested checklist (input, output, tool calls, thinking, providers, models, error rate, cache hit, total input, input cached, input uncached, tokens out, turns with tools) — plus a web-search field set\n- **Categorization**: group by provider / period / model / key, with selectable order (e.g. Provider → Period → Model)\n- **Full DB**: the 500-row page cap is bypassed; exports stream the entire matching set via keyset pagination (no OOM)\n\nPlus **site persistence**: the active view, the Analytics auto-refresh toggle + interval, and the Web Search period are saved to `localStorage` and restored on refresh. The onboarding \"Get Started\" force still wins on a fresh install.\n\n## Backend\n\n- `GET /admin/api/export` (loopback-guarded), `StreamingResponse` fed by a sync generator (Starlette threadpool keeps SQLite off the event loop)\n- `core/export.py`: field registry + per-format renderers (CSV with BOM, XLSX via openpyxl `write_only` + spool, TXT readable report, JSON array-wrapped stream)\n- `RequestLogStore.iter_export_rows` / `iter_export_aggregates` + websearch equivalents: keyset pagination over `(ts_epoch, id)`, single connection closed in `finally`, bodies decompressed only when selected\n- `openpyxl` added as a dependency; version bumped 5.1.2 → 5.2.0\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/api/test_admin_export.py`: formats, fields, grouping order, period windows, 600-row full-DB bypass, loopback guard, disabled store, web-search scope\n- `tests/core/test_export.py`: iterator paging through 650 rows, body decompression gating, aggregate grouping, web-search detail/aggregate\n- Static contract: export modal ids + label + persistence functions in `test_admin.py`; `\"Export\"` added to `DOCUMENTED_CONTROLS` (docs updated to match)\n\nFull suite: **3690 passed** (26 new), 16 pre-existing PowerShell installer/uninstaller failures identical to unmodified main.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `format=json` detail is an array-wrapped streamed document; the client downloads the Blob with zero parsing. Very large exports with bodies can produce tens-of-MB files — acceptable locally.\n- Aggregate mode rejects raw-text-only fields (web-search query/input/output) with a 400; the UI's default field set avoids them.\n- `openpyxl` is a new dependency; it is locked in `uv.lock` with the version bump.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
