    },
    "message": "feat(export): streaming analytics export endpoint with JSON/CSV/XLSX/TXT\n\nThe dashboard's Export JSON buttons only fetched the first 500 rows of the\nrequest log, so a full database could never be exported and there was no way\nto pick formats, fields, or grouping. This adds a single loopback-guarded\nGET /admin/api/export endpoint that streams the entire matching row set,\nbypassing the 500-row cap.\n\nBackend pieces:\n- core/export.py: field registry (the user's exact request field list),\n  per-format renderers (CSV, XLSX via openpyxl write_only + spool, TXT\n  readable report, JSON array-wrapped stream), and the aggregate SELECT\n  builders. Store-agnostic so it stays inside core's import boundary.\n- RequestLogStore.iter_export_rows / iter_export_aggregates and the\n  WebSearchLogStore equivalents: keyset pagination over (ts_epoch, id) so a\n  full export is O(n) instead of O(n^2) on OFFSET, single connection closed\n  in finally, bodies decompressed only when body fields are selected.\n- api/admin_export_routes.py: StreamingResponse fed by a sync generator\n  (Starlette threadpool), scope requests|websearch, group_by in output\n  order, since/until as ISO or epoch, pass-through filters.\n\nVersion bump 5.1.2 -> 5.2.0 (new capability: multi-format full-DB export) and\nuv lock with the new openpyxl dependency in the same commit.\n\nVerified: full 4-format smoke export against a seeded store (JSON rows,\nCSV with BOM, TXT report, XLSX parse, grouped records ordered\nprovider->period->model); 168 existing store/admin/boundary tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
