    "message": "feat(export): export window UI + dashboard state persistence\n\nThe two \"Export JSON\" buttons become a single \"Export\" button that opens a\ndedicated export window (modal) covering both Model requests and Web Search\nscopes. The window offers JSON/CSV/XLSX/TXT formats, a selectable period\n(hour/24h/7d/30d/custom from-to), group-by with selectable dimension order\n(provider/period/model/key), and the user's exact field checklist. It calls\nthe new GET /admin/api/export endpoint and downloads the streamed blob.\n\nSite persistence: the active view plus the analytics auto-refresh toggle,\ninterval and the web-search period are saved to localStorage\n(\"mcc-dashboard-state\") and restored on refresh, so an F5 picks the user back\nup where they were. The onboarding force still wins on a fresh install; real\nnavigation is never persisted as get_started.\n\nFrontend pieces:\n- index.html: exportModal (reuses the requests-modal dialog pattern), button\n  labels Export JSON -> Export.\n- admin.js: EXPORT_FIELDS registry, openExportModal/closeExportModal/\n  trapExportModalFocus, runExport (builds the endpoint URL, streams to a\n  blob), downloadBlob (generalized download helper, downloadJson kept as a\n  thin wrapper), DASH_STATE_KEY + persistDashboardState/restoreDashboardState\n  hooked into setActiveView and the auto-refresh/period change listeners.\n- admin.css: export-* styles (outside the contract-test prefix scan).\n\nVerified in a real browser against a throwaway server: the modal opens with\nall 13 request fields, CSV and XLSX downloads fire with correct params, and\npersisting web_search + auto-refresh restores on reload (activeView, the\ncheckbox and the interval all come back).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
