    "message": "test(export): export endpoint + iterators coverage; docs; derived-column fixes\n\nAdds the test suite for the v5.2.0 export feature and the dashboard\npersistence, and the docs lines naming the Export control.\n\nTests:\n- tests/api/test_admin_export.py: format coverage (JSON/CSV/XLSX/TXT with\n  correct content types and Content-Disposition), field selection, grouped\n  output ordering (provider->period->model), period windows (epoch + ISO),\n  a 600-row full-DB export proving the 500-row cap bypass, loopback guard,\n  disabled-store {\"enabled\": false}, and the web-search scope via the\n  get_websearch_log_store dependency override.\n- tests/core/test_export.py: iter_export_rows keyset paging through 650 rows\n  without dupes, body decompression only when body fields are selected,\n  aggregate grouping/ordering, web-search detail + aggregate iterators.\n- tests/api/test_admin.py: static contract for the export modal ids, the\n  export-button label, the persistence functions/key, and downloadBlob.\n- tests/contracts/test_docs_ui_labels.py: \"Export\" added to DOCUMENTED_CONTROLS;\n  docs/USAGE.md and the in-dashboard Guide now name the export window.\n\nBug fixes surfaced by the tests:\n- Derived aggregate columns (error_rate / cache_hit_rate) were computed on the\n  raw row then dropped by the output projection; the route now emits them.\n  _REQUEST_AGGREGATE_DERIVED values were bare strings, so iterating them split\n  into characters (\"error_rate\" -> e,r,o,_,...); now tuples.\n- websearch iter_export_rows force-includes ts_epoch/id/content_captured, which\n  _attempt_dict needs unconditionally and keyset pagination requires.\n- The websearch export path now uses the get_websearch_log_store dependency\n  (overridable in tests) instead of calling get_shared_store() directly.\n\nFull suite: 3690 passed (up from the 3663 baseline with the 26 new tests), 16\npre-existing PowerShell installer/uninstaller failures identical to unmodified\nmain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
